{"body":"The campaign currently proposes competing owners for the Asahi EBIOS tablet family. Reconcile their source scopes before integration; the evidence below does not establish identical historical excipients or authorize a maintained-owner merge.\n\n- Worker01 `KG26-PROP-172-IDENTITY` promotes existing `data/ingredients/unmapped/EBIOS.yaml` from `UNMAPPED_0380` to `kgmicrobe.ingredient:ebios`. Its payload SHA256 is `ad84636fcfdfa606ce97d7655145ed968b3c0d36e2387b5ccad1850245ffe91b`.\n- Worker02 `a2-proposal-nbrc1132-asahi-ebios-tablets` proposes a new `kgmicrobe.ingredient:nbrc1132_asahi_ebios_tablets` owner. Its payload SHA256 is `3275012aad49e7d7e353507d106a3a26c8b2313fad80e5e587ade3bec857bc3c`. Its rationale treats the existing EBIOS owner as an unresolved EBIOS/P2G record.\n- The existing owner's before hash is `130f1d9a20d6e16b9a10939a7251242d290bc8b13eb2a140be697e7b86cf87a4`. Its creation history identifies MediaDive ingredient1953. That exact frozen source record explicitly says dried yeast tablets, 10g. P2G occurs in inherited research prose and does not replace this source continuity.\n\n[JCM969](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=969) identifies EBIOS dried yeast tablets, 10g, with an Asahi Food & Healthcare footnote. Worker06 case92/TOGOM1019 is this same source context. The frozen NBRC1132 context in worker02 identifies Asahi Breweries tablets distributed by Tanabe. These facts require a reviewed product-family/source boundary decision; different recipe identifiers alone do not establish distinct product identities, and different historical supplier wording does not prove equal formulations.\n\nThe worker06 bounded finding receipt is `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-06/successor-v3/research-b/ebios-cross-shard-finding.json`, SHA256 `0fa69e99e546e64f0f7577efd9bef50114db34a7c705231c513479079311e9fd`. It preserves both exact proposal objects and payloads, all three frozen source cases, original owner history and JCM969 capture provenance. The original JCM969 capture SHA256 is `e0a5b7970d48f4ec47c071f9f21eb039465e95b58ca05efb3a4ed9a69508a1ca`, retrieved `2026-11-08T05:07:06.324562+00:00`.\n\nRequired outcome: check the established owner first; reconcile the uninstalled proposals with all author lineages and exact source links retained. Keep tablet form separate from P2G/yeast extract, preserve unknown historical excipients and doses, and avoid a global bare-brand alias. Worker06 can independently propose its exact JCM969/tablet scope against the existing owner, with this cross-shard dependency explicit. The coordinator must independently review the eventual combined payload and source applicability before application or release.\n\nThis was found during issue1217's authorized bounded EBIOS work and is filed before the worker06 EBIOS correction. An all-state read of 679 issue titles/bodies found EBIOS only in issue1217, which does not resolve this cross-worker owner conflict. No other worker was edited; no maintained change or merge has occurred.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHgiCw","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The completed W05 preparation comparison BIO-F01 positively identifies the same named Asahi EBIOS tablet family across JCM969/MediaDive1953 and NBRC1132. The existing EBIOS record's authentic creation source is1953; use that preimage/history as the continuity anchor when reconciling entries66/113 and the later W06 tablet proposal. Receiving10g versus1g doses and company/distributor wording do not establish different tablet preparations. Preserve both case lineages, literal raw labels, doses, product-history limits and all prior events; do not import P2G or current excipients as historical fact. The W06 addition was outside the frozen selected family and requires exact successor review. This reuses1221 and authorizes no maintained merge or release.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T07:30:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1221#issuecomment-6718759435","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1221,"state":"OPEN","title":"Reconcile competing Asahi EBIOS tablet proposal owners before campaign integration","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1221"}
